{"availability":"available","full":"nkhitrov/arch-blueprint","name":"arch-blueprint","description":"Render your project components automatically","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":60,"forks":5,"created":"2025-11-06T12:41:37Z","updated":"2026-10-11T16:30:52Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"","topics":["architecture","plantuml","plantuml-generator","project-structure"],"demo":"https://play.d2lang.com/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-13T02:11:38.094Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-13T02:11:38.094Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-13T02:11:38.094Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T16:43:35.468Z","stars":60,"forks":5},{"at":"2026-10-13T02:11:38.094Z","stars":60,"forks":5}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Draws the import graph of a Python project as an architecture diagram, in PlantUML or D2 source or as a PNG. It also shows what a branch changed in that graph, and how the graph grew commit by commit.","Each box is a module. An arrow means a module on one side imports a module on the other. Arrows are drawn between packages, at the level where the two modules' paths part (app2.service → app1.models is drawn as app2 → app1). A red double arrow is a cycle: two packages that import each other.","Boxes can be classes and functions too, with arrows between them (--links class)."],"features":["Choosing what to draw","Commands: draw, diff, history"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/nkhitrov/arch-blueprint/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"066acf888a5dce8bea6e664a1f4c2a4cfebfb27d133e97f26d3dd0dcd1904d0d","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:35.601Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:35.601Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Draws the import graph of a Python project as an architecture diagram, in PlantUML or D2 source or as a PNG. It also shows what a branch changed in that graph, and how the graph grew commit by commit.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/nkhitrov/arch